# Event-only seat wake

**Invariant:** `wake(IDE ∨ house seat) ⇒ real_event`; `¬wake(idle_timer)`. Digests are deduped and rate-limited. `decision:ide-house-seats-event-only-wake-and-digest-rate-limit` (`a:39651`).

| Layer | Rule |
|---|---|
| **liaison-ticker / gear-3** | No tick, spawn, or digest publish during overnight quiet (default 23:00–07:00 local, `LIAISON_OVERNIGHT_QUIET=1`). Skip the wake when the house has no open `REQUEST` and no real event. |
| **Real wake events** | **land** (worker closeout), **VERDICT** / review apply, **blocker** (`FAILED`, `BLOCKED`, `OPERATOR_GATE`, `HOLD_MERGE`, `checks_failed`), **new REQUEST** — ¬ idle `checkpoint_due`, ¬ `--heartbeat` / 20 min timers, ¬ `ORIENTED`-only churn. |
| **Attended `--loop`** | `--heartbeat` default **0**. Emit `AGENT_LOOP_TICK_liaison` only when the digest changed and a real event or fresh context-budget stop is present. |
| **DIGEST publish** | Semantic content-hash dedupe across ticks/processes; minimum interval default **300s** (`LIAISON_DIGEST_MIN_INTERVAL_S`). `publish_if_enabled(..., require_change=True)` on ticker loops. |

Code: `libs/bus_watch/spawn_on_wake.py` · `scripts/liaison-tick.py` · `libs/bus_watch/digest_publish.py`. Liaison IDE hop successors attach watcher tails only — no idle heartbeat re-arm (`liaison-hop-retire_ulg.mdc`).
